      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Historical Village at Highway 100 and Deer Ridge Road preserves Fairview’s early 19th‑century heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://franklinis.com/visit-fairview-tn-your-guide-to-attractions-and-events/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Caney Fork Furnace, built in 1832 by Moses Speer, remains Williamson County’s only surviving iron furnace and is on the National Register.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://franklinis.com/visit-fairview-tn-your-guide-to-attractions-and-events/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Bowie Nature Park spans roughly 722 acres, making it one of Tennessee’s largest city‑managed parks.",
